<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Fellner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1807">1807</a>–<a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Fellner was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> lawyer and politician who was senior mayor of the Free City of Frankfurt when Prussian troops occupied it in July 1866. Faced with a huge Prussian war levy and threats against the city, he took his own life on 24 July 1866. His death became a symbol of Frankfurt's resentment at its annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p></div>
